        "**Reasoning**:\n",
        "The `LinAlgError: Singular matrix` occurs during the conversion of `ase.Atoms` to `pymatgen.core.Structure` for isolated molecules. This typically indicates that the `Atoms` object, lacking an explicit cell definition for a non-periodic system, leads to a degenerate lattice matrix when interpreted by Pymatgen. To fix this, I will modify the `get_molecule` function to explicitly set `pbc=False` for molecules and use `atoms.center(vacuum=10.0)` to automatically create a sufficiently large, non-degenerate cell around the molecule. Additionally, I will perturb all three coordinates (x, y, z) for better initial symmetry breaking.\n",
        "\n"
